# §147 — correlated augmented-defect cancellation

Define

\[
\Delta_{ad}:=\sum_r(a_r-d_r),
\qquad
A_*:=\sum_r(a_r-T_r),
\qquad
Q_*:=\sum_rQ_r^+,
\]

and

\[
r_{deep}:=m-T\ge0.
\]

The current post-126 ledgers give the exact finite identity

\[
\boxed{
A_*-Q_*=2k+2r_{deep}+4c_I-4.
}
\tag{147.1}
\]

Proof: canonical Section 123 gives

\[
d_{tile}=q-2-a+2c_I,
\]

so

\[
a=q-2+2c_I-d_{tile}.
\]

The audited Type-II hull-side theorem gives

\[
e_{BB}=q-m=Q+2k+u_B.
\]

Section §130 gives `r_deep=m-T`, while §128 gives

\[
Q_*=Q+u_B-r_{deep}-2(c_I-1)-d_{tile}.
\]

Then

\[
A_*=a-T
=e_{BB}+r_{deep}+2c_I-2-d_{tile},
\]

and substituting `Q+u_B=e_{BB}-2k` in the expression for `Q_*` makes both `e_BB` and
`d_tile` cancel, proving (147.1).

Merged augmented-route compression gives the Type-II return floor

\[
\liminf {1\over D}
\left(\Delta_{ad}+{A_*\over2}+3Q_*\right)
\ge
{\pi\over4}(2-\sqrt3).
\tag{147.2}
\]

Using (147.1),

\[
\Delta_{ad}+{A_*\over2}+3Q_*
=
\Delta_{ad}+{7\over2}Q_*+k+r_{deep}+2c_I-2.
\]

Canonical Section 75 has `c_I=o(D)`, so

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {1\over D}
\left(
\Delta_{ad}+{7\over2}Q_*+k+r_{deep}
\right)
\ge
{\pi\over4}(2-\sqrt3).
}
\tag{147.3}
\]

In particular, if `Q_*/D`, `k/D`, and `r_deep/D` are each at most `eta`
asymptotically, then

\[
\boxed{
\liminf{\Delta_{ad}\over D}
\ge
{\pi\over4}(2-\sqrt3)-{11\over2}\eta.
}
\tag{147.4}
\]

This is an exhaustive first-order currency split, not a closure theorem.

